"Adds two numbers stored as linked lists of digits, ones digit first, as in the"
"Add Two Numbers puzzle: 342 is the list 2, 4, 3."

"One digit, and the node holding the next one (unset at the end of a list)."
type ListNode is object
    value as number
    next as maybe ListNode

function add_two_numbers takes
    first as maybe ListNode,
    second as maybe ListNode,
giving maybe ListNode
    head as ListNode is object value is 0
    tail is head
    carry is 0
    while first or second or carry > 0
        digit_one is maybe first:value otherwise 0
        digit_two is maybe second:value otherwise 0
        sum is carry + digit_one + digit_two
        carry is Math:floor (sum / 10)
        node is object value is sum mod 10
        tail:next is node
        tail is node
        first is maybe first:next
        second is maybe second:next
    return head:next

"A linked list of digits, ones digit first."
function linked takes digits as list of number, giving maybe ListNode
    head as ListNode is object value is 0
    tail is head
    for each digit in digits
        node is object value is digit
        tail:next is node
        tail is node
    return head:next

"A linked list's digits as a list."
function digits_in takes list as maybe ListNode, giving list of number
    digits is array
    while list
        digits:push list:value
        list is list:next
    return digits

"342 + 465 = 807, and 999 + 1 = 1000."
print digits_in (add_two_numbers (linked (2, 4, 3)), (linked (5, 6, 4)))
print digits_in (add_two_numbers (linked (9, 9, 9)), (linked (1,)))
